SIMONIS@stpc.wi.LeidenUniv.nl (Kris) writes:

>o btw has anyone ever noticed how powerfull a tourist gets when he completes 
>his quest? a wand of death and the yendorian Express Card...

Maybe the power of recharging should be toned down a bit (like in the
game of moria). Every time you recharge a wand, there should be a
(small) chance that the wand will explode (like a WoW always does when
you try to re-recharge it).

A possible calculation could be: cost/10 % chance of having the wand
explode (the cost of a wand varies from 100 for light and nothing to
500 for wishing and death).

This would be very easy to implement, I guess, and would limit the
extreme power of the Platimum Yendorian Express Card.

Of course, the chance could be made somewhat lower, by making the
chance, for example, cost/20.

Alternatively, the chance of a scroll of recharging appearing could be
made somewhat greater if there is a chance of evaporating a wand when
you recharge it.

By the way, I don't think the special treatment of the Wand of Wishing
should be changed. It is ok as it is now.

Since I read somewhere that proposed changes stand a better chance if
you make the change yourself and send the patched source to the dev
team, I hereby propose the change, already written into the source code.

Boudewijn.

